#Column() → Defines a column in a table.
#Integer, String, Float, TIMESTAMP, VARCHAR → Data types for columns.


#create_engine() → Connects Python to your database.

#sessionmaker() → Factory for creating database sessions (like transactions).

#declarative_base() → Base class for your table classes (all table classes must inherit from this).

#engine = create_engine(DATABASE_URL)
#Session = sessionmaker(bind=engine)
#Base = declarative_base()


#engine → actual connection to the database.

#Session() → used to talk to the database (CRUD operations).

#Base.metadata.create_all(engine) → creates all tables in the database.



